  "outcome": "upheld",
  "reason": "The clause explicitly states 'No whitespace is allowed around the `=` or inside a spec, so `bytes = 0-1` and `bytes=0 - 1` are not valid,' and the Malformed Headers section requires such invalid headers to be ignored entirely, returning the whole representation `[(0, length-1)]`. The observed result `[(0, 1)]` shows whitespace was tolerated as a parseable range instead of being rejected, directly contradicting the spec.",
  "spec_supports_expectation": true
}
